&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brunswick Group is seeking a director with strong financial communications expertise and deep experience advising clients in the Technology, Media &amp;amp; Telecommunications&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;(TMT) sector. This individual will play a significant role in delivering high-impact strategic advice to senior executives and boards, while supporting the growth of our TMT and financial communications practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Directors at Brunswick are trusted advisers, working in close partnership with clients to navigate critical issues, shape reputation, and deliver clear and compelling communications to a wide range of stakeholders, including investors, media, regulators, and employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior counsellor to clients, providing strategic financial&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;communications advice on capital markets activity, financial results, M&amp;amp;A, shareholder activism, and other complex financial situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead day-to-day client engagement for TMT sector accounts, drawing on deep knowledge of industry trends, established networks in the sector, and understanding of investor priorities and regulatory considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage teams to deliver high-quality, insight-driven work across financial, corporate, and crisis communications mandates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with CEOs, CFOs, IR leads, and senior communications executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new business opportunities by identifying growth areas, contributing to pitches, and deepening relationships within the TMT sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop junior colleagues, fostering a collaborative and high-performing team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute thought leadership on emerging issues affecting the TMT industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record (10+ years) of advising senior executives on financial&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;communications, investor relations, or capital markets engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in TMT, with direct experience advising companies in technology, media, or telecommunications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage complex projects under pressure and deliver clear, strategic, and actionable advice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wide ranging and dynamic network across the industry, media and sector participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing, presentation, and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the investor landscape, equity markets, and financial disclosure requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset with the ability to identify opportunities and contribute to business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative leadership style, with experience developing and managing diverse teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether you are joining a client facing team, a core services team, or starting out on your professional career journey, joining Brunswick unlocks a range of&amp;nbsp; employee benefits to support your financial future, health and wellness, family and community and continuous professional development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;About Brunswick&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brunswick is a global advisory firm. We help companies tackle high-stakes issues, navigate complex stakeholder relationships, and deliver high-impact outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our clients value our ability to anticipate, shape, and respond to the key players and forces in the financial and investment arena, regulatory and geopolitical universe, NGO community, workforce and beyond. They rely on us for deep experience, fresh perspectives and original thinking. So, in Brunswick you will find an exceptional range of experience and talent with a rich mix of backgrounds. From the beginning, we have prioritized attracting, developing, and retaining the best professionals in the industry, united by a culture of inclusivity, excellence, and intellectual curiosity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 1987 in London, the firm has organically grown to 27 offices in 18 countries across the Americas, Europe, Middle East, Africa, Asia and Australia. We operate as a “one-firm firm” with no individual profit centers. This allows us to assemble fully integrated, bespoke teams for each client, able to draw on the full resources of Brunswick anywhere in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Brunswick is an equal opportunity employer. &amp;nbsp;All qualified applicants will be considered without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, disability, pregnancy, genetic information, or any other status protected by applicable law. Please&amp;nbsp;read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.brunswickgroup.com/app/uploads/Group-Privacy-Notice-for-Employees_April-2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; to understand how your data is managed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
